  "native_observations": [
    "Probe compiles and invokes actual pinned TreeNode::Gemmate for both an original leaf and an original branch. It does not substitute a synthetic implementation.",
    "Trace begins at assignment into the known parent bounds address. It intentionally excludes preceding child allocation/default construction/assignment phases and non-parent bound parameter lifetimes.",
    "Successful selected phase trace is AB99,NO0,AO0,DO0: parent bounds assignment, default object temporary construction, assignment into parent object, then temporary destruction.",
    "A bounds-assignment failure records AB99 and preserves the original parent object while published children remain. A default-object construction failure records AB99,NO0 with no completed temporary to destroy.",
    "An object-assignment failure records AB99,NO0,AO0,DO0; the fixture mutates before throwing, so parent object is already zero and the temporary is destroyed during unwind.",
    "Native object assignment callback asserts that its self-address equals the retained parent object address. Rust records that comparison; parent-bound address selects the start of the phase trace.",
    "Every success/failure row checks both child parent links and, for a former branch, the reparented grandchildren. Rust additionally clears the resulting graph and verifies that its incremental allocator can reset.",
    "Fixture destructors do not throw. The oracle proves only the selected retained-parent phase and defined assignment/default exception prefixes, not full Gemmate lifetime parity."
  ],
